.TH MIRROR-DEDUPE-SCAN 1 "July 2026" "mirror-dedupe 1.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mirror-dedupe-scan \- generate repository configuration for mirror-dedupe (invoked as \fBmirror-dedupe \-\-scan\fR)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-scan
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-dest
.IR DEST ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-U
.IR URL .\|.\|.]
.RB [ \-r
.IR DIST ]
.RB [ \-R
.IR DISTS ]
.RB [ \-\-arch
.IR ARCH ]
.RB [ \-\-architectures
.IR ARCHES ]
.RB [ \-\-component
.IR COMPONENT ]
.RB [ \-\-components
.IR COMPS ]
.RB [ \-\-repo-type
.IR TYPE ]
.RB [ \-G
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-collapse-dists | \-\-no-collapse-dists ]
.RB [ \-\-emit-json ]
.RB [ \-\-no-filter ]
.RI [ UPSTREAM-URL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-scan
probes a Debian/Ubuntu repository upstream, discovers its available
distributions, architectures, and components, and generates a YAML
configuration file suitable for use with
.BR mirror-dedupe .
.PP
The generated file is written to \fB\-\-out\fR/\fINAME\fB.conf\fR.
Copy it to repos-available/ and enable via \fBmirror-dedupe \-\-activate\fR.
.PP
This replaces the former standalone \fBmirror-dedupe-scan\fR binary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Repository name (required).  Used as the config filename and the default
destination path when \fB\-\-dest\fR is omitted.
.TP
.BR \-\-dest " " \fIDEST\fR
Destination path relative to mirror_root/repos.  Defaults to \-\-name.
.TP
.BR \-\-out " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory for the generated config (required).
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-upstream " " \fIURL\fR
Upstream URL(s).  May be specified multiple times for mirror fallbacks.
The first URL is the primary; subsequent entries are used when the
primary is unreachable.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-dist ", " \-\-release " " \fIDIST\fR
Add a distribution/suite.  May be specified multiple times.  When any
\fB\-r\fR/\fB\-\-dist\fR/\fB\-\-release\fR/\fB\-R\fR option is given, the
scanner uses exactly those suites.  The special value "all" writes every
discovered suite into the config and disables automatic distribution
expansion.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-collapse-dists
Do not collapse discovered distributions; emit all variants explicitly.
.TP
.BR \-\-emit-json
Emit a JSON snapshot file alongside the YAML configuration.  The snapshot
contains the full repository structure as parsed from the upstream, which
can be useful for debugging or manual inspection.  When omitted (default)
only the YAML config is written.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-filter
Ignore architecture filters from the global \fBmirror-dedupe.conf\fR and
emit every architecture discovered upstream.  By default, architectures
listed in the global config are used as a mask \*(em any architecture not
in that list is dropped from the generated config.  This flag disables that
mask entirely, writing all discovered architectures regardless of the
global setting.
.TP
.BR \-\-repo-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Force a specific repo type (e.g. "apt") for unusual repository layouts.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gpg-key-url " " \fIURL\fR
Explicit GPG key URL for this repository.  The scanner checks that the
URL is reachable before writing the config.  The key itself is not
downloaded by the sync pipeline — the operator should fetch and verify
it separately.
.TP
.BR \-\-collapse-dists
Collapse discovered distributions to base suites where possible (e.g.
"noble-updates" becomes "noble" with automatic expansion).
.TP
.IR UPSTREAM-URL
Upstream repository URL to scan.  May also be specified via \fB\-U\fR.
.SH AUTO\-DETECTION
.PP
When no explicit dist/release/arch/component flags are given, the scanner:
.IP \(bu 3
Lists available distributions by probing the upstream's \fBdists/\fR
directory via HTML directory listing.
.IP \(bu 3
Parses architectures and components from each selected suite's
\fBRelease\fR file.
.IP \(bu 3
Behaves as if \fB\-\-releases all\fR was specified — writes every
discovered suite into the config explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan Ubuntu noble:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-scan \-\-name ubuntu \-\-release noble \-\-out /etc/mirror-dedupe/repos-available http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu
.TP
Scan a third-party repo with GPG key:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-scan \-\-name grafana \-\-out /etc/mirror-dedupe/repos-available \-\-gpg-key-url https://apt.grafana.com/gpg.key https://apt.grafana.com
.TP
Scan with multiple upstreams and custom component:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-scan \-\-name debian \-\-release bookworm \-\-component main \-\-out /tmp/scan \-\-upstream https://ftp.debian.org/debian https://mirror.yandex.ru/debian
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mirror-dedupe/repos-available/
Directory for generated repository configurations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mirror-dedupe (1)
